        "description": "Expose image frames as symlinks, decoding HEIC inputs to real lossless PNG files.",
        "category": [
          "basic",
          "input",
          "images-array-source"
        ],
        "docs": "Read-only image source bundled with HoloLab; frames_path and the frames\noutput contract are unchanged. HEIC requires Pillow and pillow-heif in the\nhost Python environment (installed with HoloLab); missing imports fail clearly.\nAccepted extensions: .png .jpg .jpeg .webp .tif .tiff .bmp .heic.\nHidden files and subdirectories are ignored. Filename byte order is preserved.\nNon-HEIC images retain their exact filenames and remain symlinks.\n.heic/.HEIC primary images become real PNGs with the same stem and\nRGB/RGBA pixels and alpha, with EXIF orientation baked into pixels.\nAll eight orientations are supported; output EXIF orientation is removed.\nNo resizing is applied. Missing or invalid orientation leaves pixels unchanged.\nICC/EXIF metadata supported by Pillow is retained. HEIC auxiliary images and\nsequences are not exported. HDR above 8 bits fails explicitly rather than\nsilently reducing precision. PNG is lossless relative to decoded HEIC pixels.\nIf suffix replacement collides or reorders frames, all HEIC outputs use\noriginal-name.heic.png (or .HEIC.png). Ambiguous fallback names fail explicitly.\nUse a fresh output directory; failed runs may leave partial outputs.\n",
